WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.206
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.832 --> 00:00:05.790
DINO CHIESA: Dino here.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.550
I'm with Apigee, which
is part of Google Cloud.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.890
This video is Apigee 101.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:12.450
We'll learn how
to create a proxy

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.130
and begin serving traffic.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.780
Let's dive in.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:22.360
After you've created your trial
account, sign in to apigee.com.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:27.380
Click the API proxies icon and
you'll see the proxies list.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.870
Now, in your
organization, you may

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.840
see one or more API proxies.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.540
What we want to do
is create a new one.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.030
We'll do that with the wizard.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:41.380
From within the wizard,
first select reverse proxy.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:45.250
We'll name the proxy,
specify a base path--

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.570
I'll say more about
that in a moment--

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.520
and specify the backend target.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.970
This is what the
proxy will connect to.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.610
For this demonstration,
we'll use a public API

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.730
that returns a JSON payload.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.430
Then we specify our
security requirements.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:05.099
For now, we will
have no security.

00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:07.230
Specify the virtual
hosts on which

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.000
this proxy will be active.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.910
I prefer the TLS-enabled v host.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:17.370
Specify the environment,
test for now.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:18.090
Done.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.290
This proxy is now active,
ready to handle traffic.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.270
Let's click through
to the proxy editor

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.700
to see the overview of
the proxy we just created.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.850
We can see all the
details we provided.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:36.680
Also, we can see the URL where
we can invoke this API proxy.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.850
Let's try it.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:41.390
Just click this URL and it
opens in another browser tab,

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.790
and we can see the JSON
returned by the proxy,

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.750
so the proxy is working.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:52.550
Let's flip back to the
Apigee administrative UI.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.560
Clicking the
Develop tab gives us

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.140
the chance to modify the
proxy produced by the wizard.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.780
I can change the deployment
status of the proxy,

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.980
undeploy it, at which point
it won't be listening anymore.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:11.400
I can change any of the
choices I made previously.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.610
And I can configure
additional policies that

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.830
will run for each
inbound request

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.740
before the request is
proxied to the target,

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.550
or policies that run on the
response after the response is

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.320
received from the
target but before it

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.550
is sent to the original client.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:32.300
Apigee proxies are
smart and configurable.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.390
Let's add a rate-limiting
policy to this proxy, a quota

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:36.590
enforcement.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:41.380
To do that, I'll click the
preflow in the proxy endpoint

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:44.890
and click the plus step icon.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.990
Here I see a list of
the various policies

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:48.730
Apigee Edge has available.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:52.110
I want the quota policy.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:55.650
Let's configure it with a fixed
rate limit of three requests

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.660
for every minute.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:01.050
To do that, I'll just paste
in some simple configuration.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.820
Then I'll save it
and redeploy it.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.880
And then, flipping back
to the other browser tab,

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.240
I can invoke it again.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.880
Now, there's no change in the
behavior of this API proxy.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.210
It's still returning JSON.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.210
But after I invoke that
proxy more than three times,

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.540
I get an error that says the
rate limit has been exceeded.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.670
The Apigee proxy is
rejecting the request

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.800
because it's
exceeding the limit.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.230
Rate limiting is easy.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.110
Flipping back to the
Apigee administrative UI,

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:39.520
in the Develop tab, let me
raise that limit to, oh, 1,000

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:40.960
requests per minute.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.470
I can do it just like that.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.050
But surely there are other
options for the quota policy.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.220
How do I learn about them?

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:54.310
By selecting the policy
in the API proxy editor,

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:56.080
I can get a hyperlink
that takes me

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.900
to the documentation
for that policy.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.790
Here I can learn
everything I need

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:06.393
to know about how to use the
quota policy, super helpful.

00:04:06.393 --> 00:04:07.810
If you have questions
that are not

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:11.200
answered by the documentation,
you can visit the community.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.360
Find the link to the
community in the Apigee

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:16.370
administrative UI.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:20.670
Search there or
ask a new question.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.160
Friendly Apigee experts
like me are always there,

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.960
willing to help you out.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.790
In this video, you
learned the basics

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.640
of Apigee Edge, how
to create an API proxy

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:32.430
and how to add a
policy to a proxy, how

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:34.260
to find documentation
on a policy

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:37.410
and how to navigate to
the Apigee community.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:41.460
In the next video, we'll cover
how to add API key verification

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.230
to an existing proxy.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:46.350
Until then, I wish
you strong API mojo.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:49.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

